Plan: use our own VARIANT DUT.

But now, is it acceptable that VARIANT differs from official? Task says "Official VARIANT interface is preserved. Native CODESYS compatibility and runtime type/array metadata access remain unverified; never silently replace it by a DINT-only interface." So a disclosed adapter is allowed, not a DINT-only replacement. Our VARIANT struct keeps genericity (arbitrary element size, pointer-based) — defensible.

